<title>USA: Texas Utilities Co Q3 shr net. [CORRECTED 19:17 GMT]</title>
<headline>Texas Utilities Co Q3 shr net. [CORRECTED 19:17 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline, which had stated that there had been a decline in profit).</p>
<p>				1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $1.59     loss	 $1.96</p>
<p> Oper shr profit	   1.59   profit	  1.59</p>
<p> Net profit	     357,983     loss     441,716</p>
<p> Revs		   1,930,097		1,775,669</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 224,603		  225,841</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $3.40     loss	 $0.81</p>
<p> Oper shr profit	   2.74   profit	  2.74</p>
<p> Net profit	     766,242     loss     182,298</p>
<p> Revs		   6,350,066		5,594,620</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 225,469		  225,841</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - 1995 net both periods includes an after-tax charge of $802 million for the writedown of impaired assets including uncompleted coal-fired generating units, coal reserves and miscellaneous other assets.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
